From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:16:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] glm5_next/cuda: noise-aware DFlash2 draft policies,
 TF_GLM_DFLASH_POLICY (MiaAI-Lab recipe patches 0018, 0021)

MiaAI-Lab's recipe (github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold @ 1576746, with
DRAFT_POLICY=fnc7:0.3 in its config) stops each round's DFlash2 chain by the chance that the target's own keyed
sample takes each draft, not by the drafter's softmax alone: fnc7:0.3 drafts up to 7 while the product of those
noise-aware confidences holds 0.3. TensorFold's default DFlash2 policy is fc5:0.3 (up to 5 while the plain product
holds 0.3). This ports recipe patches 0018-glm-noise-policies and 0021-glm-dflash-policy-env (Apache License 2.0,
Copyright 2026 MiaAI-Lab), with the multi-stream parts of 0027/0030/0035 that carry them, at their end state:

- dflash2.py: NOISY_BETA (2.0, fitted in the recipe), noisy_confidence (softmax((score + g) / beta) at the pick, g
  the target's keyed Gumbel draws; none when greedy), best_depth (the depth maximizing expected tokens per ms).
  Drafter.chain and Drafter.propose take beta and round_ms; only where a chain stops changes, never its picks. The
  joint allocation's confidences are noise-aware when the policy has a beta.
- engine.py: encode_policy reads fncN:P[:B] (kind 16) and fcostN:noisy[:B] (kind 17, the depth that maximizes
  E[tokens] / round ms by the startup cost table); decode_policy(code, costs) and round_costs. N goes up to 7, the
  drafts of the verify windows _calibrate times here (1 to 8 rows; the recipe bounds it by its captured windows,
  also 7). TF_GLM_DFLASH_POLICY sets the DFlash2 policy auto requests run on an EXL3 checkpoint with the draft model
  (DFLASH_POLICY, read at import; unset = fc5:0.3); a value that is not a DFlash2 policy is refused at startup, and
  on the attention/expert split's attention node before the wire opens.
- decode.py: DepthPolicy carries beta and round_ms (chain_rule); dflash_decode proposes with them.
- dflash2_multi.py and multi.py (PR #243's engine): DraftRequest carries the rule to MultiDrafter.propose; each
  stream's policy decodes with the cost table; MTP twins keep the MTP rule.

Drafts only propose: the verify window's keyed samples decide every token, so replies are unchanged under any
policy; the policy changes how many rows each round verifies. Unset, TF_GLM_DFLASH_POLICY is fc5:0.3 and every
request's drafts and replies are the ones before. On the split each extra verified row costs more than on two Sparks
(measured a layer on its expert nodes: 1.07 ms at 8 rows, 1.95 ms at 15, 3.05 ms at 27), so the gain needs an A/B
on the split's hardware.

Tests: tests/test_glm_draft_policy.py (CPU): the recipe's units, verbatim in tests/glm_draft_policy_mia.py and pinned
by sha256, against ours (noisy_confidence, best_depth, round_costs, _encode_noisy's codes and refusals, chain under
every rule); the base's specs encode as before; the setting read at import and refused before the wire; PR #243's
fake model with the real MultiDrafter.propose and Drafter.chain over fake candidates: drafted replies equal serial
ones under fc5:0.3, fnc7:0.3, fnc7:0.6:1.0, fnc3:0.0, fcost7:noisy, fcost5:noisy:3 and f3, one stream and 2/4
streams at two ranks (both ranks agree), PR #243's staggered requests under the setting, TF_GLM_KV=fp8's rings, world
1 over the fake AFD wire, the joint allocation.

Credit: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md ("GLM noise-aware DFlash2 draft policies") and the ported units' comments name
MiaAI-Lab and the patches.

